>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `register_ersatz`

``` hol4
Refute.register_ersatz :
  {original : {Thy : string, Name : string},
   replacement : {Thy : string, Name : string}} -> unit
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Adds or replaces one model-finder constant substitution.

When preprocessing encounters the named `original` constant, Refute
instantiates the named `replacement` constant to the original occurrence's
type and uses it in the relational encoding.  A later session-local row
with the same original theory/name key replaces the old ordinary row and
also shadows a built-in ordinary row.

An active fraction registration has higher precedence than ordinary
ersatz rows.  Thus a colliding `register_ersatz` row is retained but does
not take effect until the fraction registration is replaced or removed.
The operation creates no HOL constant or theorem.

Registration does not eagerly resolve either name or check type
compatibility.  An absent constant or a replacement that cannot be
retyped is reported when model-finder preprocessing uses the row.

### See also

[`Refute.register_frac_type`](#Refute.register_frac_type),
[`Refute.register_frac_type_rat`](#Refute.register_frac_type_rat),
[`Refute.register_term_postprocessor`](#Refute.register_term_postprocessor),
[`Refute.model_refute`](#Refute.model_refute)

Model-finder preprocessing is described in
\ref{Description:the-holrefute-library}.
